### Backend Profiling

Look for these patterns:

| Problem                    | What to Look For                                                        |
| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| N+1 queries                | Loops issuing individual queries instead of joins or eager loading       |
| Missing indexes            | Columns used in WHERE, JOIN, ORDER BY without indexes                   |
| No pagination              | Endpoints returning all records without limit/offset                    |
| Heavy serialization        | Models loading unnecessary relationships during serialization           |
| Sync blocking I/O          | File uploads, email sending, or external calls not using async          |
| Missing cache              | Frequently queried, rarely changing data with no cache layer            |
| Uploads without streaming  | Large files loaded entirely into memory instead of streamed             |
<% } %>
<% if (modules.mobile || modules.web) { %>

### Frontend Profiling

| Problem                     | What to Look For                                                       |
| --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
<% if (mobileFramework === 'expo-rn-nativewind' || mobileFramework === 'flutter') { %>
| Unnecessary re-renders      | Components re-rendering without prop or state changes                  |
| Lists without virtualization| FlatList/ListView missing optimization, large lists without windowing   |
| Unoptimized images          | No resize, compression, or caching strategy for images                 |
<% } %>
| Bundle bloat                | Heavy imports without lazy loading or code splitting                   |
| Memory leaks                | Event listeners or subscriptions not cleaned up                        |
| Heavy screens               | Complex screens loaded eagerly instead of lazily                       |
<% } %>

### Network Profiling

| Problem              | What to Look For                                                   |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Redundant requests   | Same endpoint called multiple times for the same data              |
| Large payloads       | Returning more fields than the client needs                        |
| No compression       | Responses without gzip/brotli                                      |
| Inadequate timeouts  | Missing or excessively long timeout configurations                 |

